OL,1,V7w3s7s35E                        G11/26
OL,2,V55555555CHELP FOR VICTIMS
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CIN CRIME CRACKDOWN
OL,4,B
OL,5, A tougher crackdown on criminals and a
OL,6, fairer deal for their victims is out-
OL,7, lined in a White Paper which will form
OL,8, the basis of a Criminal Justice Bill.
OL,10, It increases sentences - to life for
OL,11, having guns - and allows seizure of
OL,12, criminals' assets to compensate victims
OL,14, The right of a trial by jury may go in
OL,15, some minor cases and there will be
OL,16, easier extradition of alleged criminals
OL,18, Home Secretary Douglas Hurd said that
OL,19, the plans were part of a developing
OL,20, strategy, but Labour's Gerald Kaufman
OL,21, called the White Paper "a few patches
OL,22, of whitewash on a disgraceful record".
OL,23,F]DFrom 06-03-96 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49612
SC,0012
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1772762637
OL,1,V7w3s7s35E                        G12/26
OL,2,V55555555CPOLICE HIT AT
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CGUN LAW CLAMPDOWN
OL,4,B
OL,5, The Police Federation has hit at the
OL,6, Criminal Justice White Paper plan to
OL,7, give judges the power to pass life
OL,8, sentences on those carrying guns.
OL,10, It said it would end the differential
OL,11, between the punishment for murder and
OL,12, for carrying a firearm, so a gunman
OL,13, would not be deterred from killing.
OL,15, Laws that lay down maximum sentences
OL,16, which will not be enforced "make a
OL,17, mockery of the life sentence", it added
OL,19, But the prisoners' group NACRO said it
OL,20, was "deeply disturbed" by the move to
OL,21, allow a review of lenient sentences and
OL,22, said jail terms should be reduced.
OL,23,F]DFrom 06-03-96 / teletextarchive.com
