OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1772762637
OL,1,Qk7jwh7}h7}j5~s"##################G23/26
OL,2,Q*%*-*%/*%/*%,'   C     USA WOMEN'S Q  j
OL,3,Q5GPrinceton, N Jersey CINDOOR CH'SHIPQj
OL,4,Q#######################################
OL,5,FMartina Navratilova took another step
OL,6,Fon the way to her expected place in
OL,7,Fthe final with an easy 6-0 6-4 second
OL,8,Fround win over Czech Andrea Holikova.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FTwo Czechs who won were Helena Sukova,
OL,11,Fwho beat Elise Burgin 6-1 6-2, and Hana
OL,12,FMandlikova, a 6-3 6-2 victor against
OL,13,FSylvia Hanika.
OL,14,F
OL,15,FBut seventh seed Barbara Potter went
OL,16,Fout 6-3 2-6 6-3 to Alycia Moulton who
OL,17,Fhad returned to action after a couple
OL,18,Fof days in bed with flu.
OL,20,FNinth seed Anne White also fell by the
OL,21,Fwayside after being beaten 6-3 6-2 by
OL,22,Fanother American, Terry Phelps.
OL,23,Q]GFrom 06-03-86 / teletextarchive.com
