OL,2,Q+.!/*%/"-'*%/*- /C  MOVES TO EASE    Qj
OL,3,Q5GTCCB MEETING    C BOUNCER PROBLEM  Qj
OL,4,Q#######################################
OL,5,FThe TCCB has made the first moves to
OL,6,Fease the umpire's interpretation of
OL,7,Fshort-pitched bowling.
OL,9,FThe Board has formulated a new wording
OL,10,Fof the law covering bouncers and it
OL,11,Fwill be passed onto the ICC for debate
OL,12,Fat their annual meeting in July.
OL,14,FMeanwhile, a call for uncovered pitches
OL,15,Fin the County Ch'ship has been rejected
OL,17,FA shoot-out in one-day matches will be
OL,18,Fbrought in next season with five
OL,19,Fplayers on each side bowling at a set
OL,20,Fof stumps when games are hit by rain.
OL,22,FFred Titmus is to succeed Alec Bedser
OL,23,Fon England's selection panel.C
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
