OL,2,Q/*%+.!+.!/.!,.!     Wj5~k4h7}h7}   Qj
OL,3,Q5CPERKINS QUITS     W+.!/*%/"-'*%/   Qj
OL,4,Q#######################################
OL,5,FWales second row forward John Perkins
OL,6,Fhas made a shock decision to quit the
OL,7,Finternational scene.
OL,9,FThe Pontypool skipper said he had four
OL,10,Fgreat years at the top.
OL,12,FPerkins, 32, added: "I feel the Welsh
OL,13,Fselectors, with their eyes on the World
OL,14,FCup, should look to younger players."
OL,16,FBut the lock, with nearly 500 games
OL,17,Fbehind him for Pontypool, stressed he
OL,18,Fwould continue to play club rugby for
OL,19,Fanother two years.
OL,21,FPerkins had the unusual distinction of
OL,22,Fwinning his 18 caps without a break.
OL,23,Q]GFrom 06-03-86 / teletextarchive.com
